From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:50:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: dw_hdmi_qp: Let the controller see DCLK stop on
 a modeset

When a modeset disables and re-enables the VOP video port driving the
HDMI controller within one commit, the VOP gates DCLK in its
.atomic_disable() and ungates it again in its .atomic_enable() right
afterwards. The HDMI controller needs about 2 ms to detect that its
video input clock stopped, and only then reinitializes its input pixel
interface.

Without that, leaving YCbCr 4:2:0 output breaks the next mode on RK3588,
e.g. switching from 4096x2160@60 YCbCr 4:2:0 to 4096x2160@60 10 bpc RGB
over FRL fails in about half of the attempts: the controller does not
lock onto the new video stream and the sink shows "no signal" while the
link itself is fine. The broken state can then survive further modesets
done this way, including plain 1080p TMDS modes, so the output looks
dead until it is disabled in a separate commit or the board is rebooted.

The encoder's .atomic_mode_set() is called after the CRTC has been
disabled and before it is enabled again, so wait there until the
controller reports the input clock as stopped. If the CRTC was already
off, the clock is already reported stopped and this returns immediately.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi_qp-rockchip.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi_qp-rockchip.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi_qp-rockchip.c
index f9b03c3ed16b..eb1b5f49bb3d 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi_qp-rockchip.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi_qp-rockchip.c
@@ -297,8 +297,24 @@ dw_hdmi_qp_rockchip_encoder_atomic_check(struct drm_encoder *encoder,
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static void
+dw_hdmi_qp_rockchip_encoder_atomic_mode_set(struct drm_encoder *encoder,
+					    struct drm_crtc_state *crtc_state,
+					    struct drm_connector_state *conn_state)
+{
+	struct rockchip_hdmi_qp *hdmi = to_rockchip_hdmi_qp(encoder);
+
+	/*
+	 * This runs after the VOP has been disabled and before it is enabled
+	 * again. Keep DCLK stopped until the controller has noticed, so that
+	 * its video input starts afresh with the new mode.
+	 */
+	dw_hdmi_qp_wait_input_clk_off(hdmi->hdmi);
+}
+
 static const struct
 drm_encoder_helper_funcs dw_hdmi_qp_rockchip_encoder_helper_funcs = {
+	.atomic_mode_set = dw_hdmi_qp_rockchip_encoder_atomic_mode_set,
 	.atomic_enable	= dw_hdmi_qp_rockchip_encoder_atomic_enable,
 	.atomic_check	= dw_hdmi_qp_rockchip_encoder_atomic_check,
 };
